        "original_id": "cfd0a93f-2949-5030-a111-ac016717a784",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Turner Field, Centennial Olympic Stadium, Atlanta\n- Organizations: Atlanta Braves\n- Events: 1996 Summer Olympics, 1996 Summer Paralympics, 2013 Atlanta Braves season\n\nFacts:\n- Centennial Olympic Stadium was an 85,000-seat main stadium for the 1996 Summer Olympic Games and the 1996 Summer Paralympic Games in Atlanta.\n- Turner Field was originally built in 1996 as Centennial Olympic Stadium to serve as the centerpiece of the 1996 Summer Olympics.\n- Turner Field was later converted into a baseball park to become the new home of the Atlanta Braves.\n- The 2013 Atlanta Braves season was the team's 17th season of home games at Turner Field, its 48th season in Atlanta, and its 143rd season overall.",
